{"id":19527,"title":"Zip-NeRF: Anti-Aliased Grid-Based Neural Radiance Fields","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/iccv51070.2023.01804","final_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.06706","year":2023,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":"10.1109/iccv51070.2023.01804","arxiv":null,"sha256":"f782e4c8381ae3fcb137d4957833f3a2d04a2240e164feb62be06ca4177a01eb","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793065083.816898,"text_chars":79815,"abstract":"Neural Radiance Field training can be accelerated through the use of\ngrid-based representations in NeRF's learned mapping from spatial coordinates\nto colors and volumetric density. However, these grid-based approaches lack an\nexplicit understanding of scale and therefore often introduce aliasing, usually\nin the form of jaggies or missing scene content. Anti-aliasing has previously\nbeen addressed by mip-NeRF 360, which reasons about sub-volumes along a cone\nrather than points along a ray, but this approach is not natively compatible\nwith current grid-based techniques. We show how ideas from rendering and signal\nprocessing can be used to construct a technique that combines mip-NeRF 360 and\ngrid-based models such as Instant NGP to yield error rates that are 8% - 77%\nlower than either prior technique, and that trains 24x faster than mip-NeRF\n360.Comment: Project page: https://jonbarron.info/zipnerf","file":null,"marks":[],"links":["https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.06706","https://doi.org/10.1109/iccv51070.2023.01804","https://core.ac.uk/download/561015449.pdf","https://arxiv.org/pdf/2304.06706v3","https://jonbarron.info/zipnerf/","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xrrhynRzC8k","https://web.archive.org/web/20260101130818/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xrrhynRzC8k"],"cited_by":[{"path":"1267-value-normalization-and-quantization.md","name":"Value Normalization and Quantization","k":19},{"path":"1267-fourier-positional-encoding.md","name":"Fourier Positional Encoding","k":19},{"path":"2484-nerf-with-per-image-embeddings.md","name":"NeRF with Per-Image Embeddings","k":2},{"path":"957-unbounded-inward-facing-scene-parameterization.md","name":"Unbounded inward-facing scene parameterization","k":1},{"path":"3457-anti-aliased-interlevel-loss.md","name":"Anti-Aliased Interlevel Loss","k":1},{"path":"3426-mip-nerf-360-optimization-setup.md","name":"Mip-NeRF 360 Optimization Setup","k":2},{"path":"2346-power-transformation.md","name":"Power Transformation","k":1},{"path":"2444-view-dependent-mlp.md","name":"View-Dependent MLP","k":1},{"path":"3498-hexagonal-multisampling-pattern-derivation.md","name":"Hexagonal Multisampling Pattern Derivation","k":1},{"path":"3030-zip-nerf.md","name":"Zip-NeRF","k":1},{"path":"5407-isotropic-gaussian-scale-contraction.md","name":"Isotropic Gaussian Scale Contraction","k":1},{"path":"2332-training-configuration.md","name":"Training Configuration","k":3},{"path":"5408-mip-nerf-360-proposal-sampling.md","name":"Mip-NeRF 360 Proposal Sampling","k":2},{"path":"7-multiresolution-and-level-of-detail.md","name":"Multiresolution and level of detail","k":4},{"path":"4560-distortion-loss-with-power-transformation.md","name":"Distortion Loss with Power Transformation","k":1},{"path":"4383-blurring-a-step-function.md","name":"Blurring a Step Function","k":1},{"path":"3497-affine-generative-latent-optimization.md","name":"Affine Generative Latent Optimization","k":1},{"path":"8571-scale-dependent-downweighting-for-grid-interpolation.md","name":"Scale-Dependent Downweighting for Grid Interpolation","k":1},{"path":"2404-ingp-hierarchy-configuration.md","name":"iNGP Hierarchy Configuration","k":1}]}